source: tests/human_output.rs
description: "Created join key on the named network, its enrollment command, the once-only warning, and the default-role note."
---
$ dn join-key create ci-runner --network network-Z2B7RBHWBP3VSDAPEWFWKMOMZU --tag env:ci --expires-at 2099-01-01T00:00:00Z
Created join key "ci-runner" (dnjoin-P3RCTXN5LVFGBMJNYF2QHKWDOA)
ID:                 dnjoin-P3RCTXN5LVFGBMJNYF2QHKWDOA
Network:            network-Z2B7RBHWBP3VSDAPEWFWKMOMZU
Role:               default role
Tags:               env:ci
Auto-assign CIDRs:  100.100.0.0/22, fd00:c0:c0::/80
Expires:            2099-01-01T00:00:00Z
Created:            2026-10-29T15:00:00Z
Modified:           2026-10-29T15:00:00Z

On each machine, install dnclient and run:
  dnclient enroll -code dnjoin-P3RCTXN5LVFGBMJNYF2QHKWDOA-6YQKZ3VNB2XGJ4MEPLRT7WCSAHDUF5IO3QXBKZNYV2MJ4RLEHGTA

The token is shown only this once; store it somewhere safe. Every machine
that enrolls with it joins as a new host.

Note: the default role denies all inbound traffic. Hosts enrolled with this
key will be on the network but unreachable until a role with firewall rules
is assigned to them (see `dn role list`), unless one of the key's tags
carries firewall rules (see `dn tag get`).
